menu "TrailCamHub: uplink"

config UPLINK_VIDEO_MAX_MB
    int "Largest video uploaded to the backend (MB)"
    depends on CAMERA_DOWNLOAD_VIDEOS
    range 1 1000
    default 50
    help
        Requested videos are uploaded as MP4, built while they are sent from
        the stored H.264 and AAC files (nothing extra is stored). A larger
        one is reported as failed.

config UPLINK_VIDEO_MAX_MB_MODEM
    int "Largest video uploaded over the cellular modem (MB)"
    depends on CAMERA_DOWNLOAD_VIDEOS && MODEM_UPLINK
    range 1 1000
    default 15
    help
        A lower limit when the hub syncs over the A7670E (setting
        "transport"): data volume and radio time. Measured with LTE Cat-1:
        about 650 KB of MP4 per second of 1080p video and about 50 KB/s
        upload, so 15 MB is a clip of ~20 s and ~5 min of transmitting. A
        larger video is answered as failed with the reason; a hub syncs
        over one transport only, so it is not kept for a Wi-Fi sync.

endmenu
